Polar Operations LLC dba IMC Markets has multiple openings for Hardware Engineer (REQ ID: 4528528101) in Chicago, IL and New York, NY.

Your Core Responsibilities

• Design, develop, and improve FPGA and ASIC features in SystemVerilog to accelerate the latency and throughput of IMC’s proprietary trading systems and their communication with U.S. financial exchanges (20%).

• Independently execute end-to-end hardware engineering projects, from conceiving proposed designs through test planning, verification, and coordinating deployment into production (10%).

• Design APIs, testing and simulation frameworks, and other C++ software features to support new hardware capabilities (20%).

• Analyze market data and existing trading system behavior to identify opportunities to improve the performance of IMC’s trading platform (10%).

• Manage the multi-vendor hardware build, test, and deployment workflow using TeamCity, and provide operational support to production trading systems by diagnosing and debugging hardware issues (10%).

• Work with Traders, Quantitative Analysts, Developers, and other Engineers to translate trading requirements into hardware and software solutions (15%).

• Mentor graduate hardware engineers and interns, and contribute to planning and prioritization of future hardware engineering projects (15%).

Partial telecommuting permitted. Multiple positions available. Requisition ID: 4528528101.

Your Skills and Experience

This position requires a Bachelor’s degree, or foreign equivalent, in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a similarly rigorous technical field, and one (1) year of experience in the job offered or a related occupation. Must have at least one (1) year of experience in each of the following skills:

• Using SystemVerilog for the design and development of ultra-low-latency and high throughput data processing applications, measured in a nano-second time scale;

• Designing, developing, and implementing complex algorithms and data structures in FPGA and/or ASIC hardware;

• Timing analysis and timing closure optimization of FPGA designs in Xilinx Vivado;

• Building custom applications with Ethernet, IP, UDP, and TCP to send and receive data to market exchanges;

• Using BGP, ARP, and IGMP to maintain connections with market exchanges;

• Working with 10G Ethernet down to the PCS layer;

• Using network analysis tools, including Wireshark and tcpdump;

• Using C++20 to support new hardware capabilities in trading systems, including the use of Verilator-based C++ unit testing frameworks to validate RTL designs;

• Using Python, SQL, and C++ to analyze the performance of existing systems and identify patterns in market data;

• Collaborating with trading desks and developing hardware for use in a quantitative trading environment; and

• Foundational knowledge of quantitative trading concepts and equity/index options.

